# Round 92: the round-91 RANGED _v wrappers hand-wrote the slice instead of
# deferring -- breaking the rule that same commit stated for the scalar
# ones ("a hand-written fallback is not faithful; the oracle answers by
# construction"). Three measured consequences, all silent-wrong: a nested
# list element was coerced to 0.0 where the VM FLATTENS (sum of a nested
# slice gave 0 vs 10); VAL_STR was called length-0 though the bt class
# carries strings; and dict/num were treated as empty containers, turning
# the VM's "cannot slice dict" into a silent 0. The slice is now a faithful
# mirror of OP_SLICE_GET -- per-type length, negative resolution, element
# VALUES not doubles, and the VM's one error text with the ORIGINAL bounds
# -- and its result goes to the runtime's own builtin.
define rs(b) as:
    return sum of b[0 : 2]
define rn(b) as:
    return norm of b[0 : 2]
xs is [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
print of (rs of xs)
print of (rn of xs)
ys is [1, 2, 3, 4]
print of (rs of ys)
print of (rn of ys)
print of (rs of "abcd")
zb is buffer of 4
zb[0] is 1
zb[1] is 2
print of (rs of zb)
print of (sum of ys[-3 : -1])
print of (sum of ys[2 : 2])
